# Button Color Hierarchy

Use this hierarchy for all user actions to keep visual consistency:

- `btn-primary`: main action (save, create, confirm)
- `btn-secondary`: neutral/secondary action (cancel, back, close) using tonal primary container
- `btn-schedule-sm`: alternative accent action (add/schedule) using tertiary container
- `btn-delete` / `btn-delete-sm` / `btn-danger`: destructive actions only

## Rules

- Do not use gray-only secondary buttons for cancel/secondary flows.
- Do not create new one-off button colors when an existing class already matches the action semantic.
- Prefer semantic class reuse over inline style color overrides.
- Keep hover behavior subtle (`filter: brightness(...)`) and based on the same palette token family.

## Examples

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD
<button className="btn-primary">Salvar</button>
<button className="btn-secondary">Cancelar</button>
<button className="btn-schedule-sm">+ Adicionar treino</button>

// ❌ BAD
<button style={{ background: '#e5e7eb', color: '#111827' }}>Cancelar</button>
<button className="btn-secondary custom-pink-btn">Adicionar</button>
```
